EXT. FROZEN WATERFALL - GORGE - DAY

A canyon of blue ice, walls streaked with silver where the water froze mid-fall. The sky is a slice of white between cliffs. Wind whistles through the cracks.

Four climbers cling to the face. Ropes run taut between them.

AUGUSTINE "AUGIE" DELACROIX-OWUSU, 30s, leads, swinging an ice axe in short, practiced arcs. Below him, THALIA RENFREW, 20s, belays on a narrow ledge, her hands sheathed in battered mittens. Further down, ZEPHANIAH "ZEPH" OKONJO, 40s, the guide, hangs from a screw with one arm. At the bottom, the youngest, QUINLAN BRADSHAW-LEE, 17, stands on the snow, waiting his turn.

                    AUGIE
(calling down)
Ice is good!

                    THALIA
Copy!

She feeds him rope. Zeph watches the line shiver. Quinlan stamps his feet.

Augie pulls over a lip and anchors himself. Looks down the face, grins.

                    AUGIE
Zeph! Your turn!

Zeph begins to climb. He moves with the slow confidence of a man who has done this ten thousand times. Axe, kick, axe, kick.

Halfway up, a CRACK splits the air.

All four freeze.

A fissure races across the ice, a bright zigzag of white, and a slab the size of a door calves off the wall above Zeph and falls.

                    THALIA
Zeph!

He flings himself sideways. The slab clips his pack and spins him. His axe slips. He swings, catches, hangs.

Augie hauls the rope in, arm over arm. Thalia braces. Quinlan scrambles up the snow slope toward the base of the wall, shouting.

                    QUINLAN
Hold on! I'm coming!

                    ZEPH
(through his teeth)
Stay down, boy!

Another crack. A second slab shakes loose, then a third. The whole sheet of ice shudders, groans, and begins to peel from the cliff like old paint.

Augie and Thalia lock eyes. Wordlessly, together, they haul with everything they have. Zeph kicks into the wall. His crampons bite. He lunges up and over the ledge as the ice behind him thunders into the gorge.

They collapse in a heap, all three tangled in rope, breathing fast.

Quinlan, at the bottom, stands in the settling snow with his hands on his head, laughing and gasping.

                    QUINLAN
That was incredible.

                    ZEPH
It was not.
